   108	## (b) Tiers as registered and as computed
   109	
   110	Plan v15 §1 (`plan_depth_canon.md:28-31`), quoted:
   111	- "**Tier 1 — structural (exact):** for every item of a rotated cell (C4, 45°, random yaw) the sha256 of the *canonical
   112	  recovered-depth image* equals the one of the same item in the θ=0 cell with the same seed and K: 6,337 / 6,337 equal".
   113	- "**Tier 2 — practical waveform invariance** … paired per-item relative L2 and L∞ between the scored waveforms of a
   114	  rotated cell and its θ=0 pair (identical eval seed ⇒ identical generative noise and context draw, proven by identical
   115	  `input_hash`) … `relL2 = ‖a−b‖₂ / max(‖b‖₂, 1e-6)` … Two controls: (i) the **determinism floor** — a duplicate θ=0
   116	  cell (same seed, run twice; expected exactly reproducible) …; (ii) the **numerical-composition control**
   117	  (`depth_canon_cond_probe.py`, GPU, fixed noise): for 64 unseen items × offsets {64, 128, 256, 384, random}, direct
   118	  `canon(md)` vs `canon(rot_d(md))` compared stagewise … **Pre-registered PASS rule:** `p99(relL2) ≤ 3 × p99` of the
   119	  composition control's waveform relL2 … **and** `p99(relL2) ≤ 1e-2` (hard cap); `max(relL2) ≤ 1e-1` is an alarm bound
   120	  … the duplicate cell must be exactly reproducible (`max relL2 == 0`)".
   121	- "**Tier 3 — metrics:** `Δ_C4(K)` = max−min over θ ∈ {0, 90, 180, 270}° (seed 42) and the 45° off-orbit probe;
   122	  `Δ_R(K) = m_R − m_Z` seed-paired over seeds 42–46 … PASS if `Δ_C4` of CANON ≤ 10 % of P1's one-pin `Δ_C4` on every
   123	  metric and `|Δ_R|` ≤ 1 eval-seed sd of `m_Z`."
   124	- ε_cond = max fp32 conditioning relL2 of the control, registered ≤ 1e-5 (measured 8.12e-5 → FAIL; Yixun: report as
   125	  registered + labelled diagnosis, adjudication A).
   126	
   127	In collect.py: **T-dup** = block `T-dup` paired with its T cell (`make_pairs` :745-746), PASS iff input_hash equal,
   128	max relL2 == 0 and dump sha256 equal (:1034-1041). **Composition control** = `load_control` (:962-986) of a registered
   129	probe JSON validated by `probe_reasons` (:915-959; `PROBE_CONTRACT` :825-832), mapping 45°→d64, 90°→d128, 180°→d256,
   130	270°→d384, random→random (`CONTROL_KEYS` :816); Tier 2 = every pair passes matched (≤ 3× its control p99) and cap
   131	(≤ 1e-2) AND the pooled rule (:1005-1049; constants :815). **Δ_C4** = max−min of the item-weighted metric over the
   132	four seed-42 θ cells, only if all four share the θ=0 input_hash (:1090, 1093, 1097); **45° probe** = v(45°) − v(0°),
   133	seed 42, signed (:1098); **Δ_R** = mean over seeds 42–46 of v(R_s) − v(T_s), only when all 5 pairs are input_hash-equal
   134	(:1094, 1099); **sd(m_Z)** = `statistics.stdev` (n−1) of the 5 θ=0 values (:1092, 1081-1084). **Item-weighted** = the
   135	record's flat `metrics` block (`_value` agg "item" :1059-1063); per-scene = mean over the 10 `by_scene` families,
   136	recorded only. Metrics: T60, C50, EDT, FD, R@1, R@5, R@10 (`TIER3_KEYS` :48-49; FD is in Tier 3 but not in Yixun's
   137	six-metric tables). Rule: `pass_c4 = Δ_C4(arm) ≤ 0.10 × Δ_C4(P1-pin)`, `pass_r = |Δ_R(arm)| ≤ sd(m_Z arm)` for every
   138	metric and both K, item-weighted (`tier3` :1103-1121, `TIER3_FRACTION` :1055); written only for CANON vs P1 today.
