   152	  (comma string, parsed at eval_FLAC.py:2282) `--frame-avg-max-fwd-samples 64` + the common flags. Record then holds
   153	  `cond_method fa_invariant, frame_avg_angles [0.0,90.0,180.0,270.0], orbit_execution "batched", frame_avg_fwd_cap 64`
   154	  (`orbit_provenance` :1304-1320, yaw_rotation.py:52,56); file stem gains `_fa_invariant_a4` (:630).
   155	  Eval chunk plan: batch 64, cap 64 → 1 angle per forward for the 99 full batches; the 1-item tail batch (6337 = 99·64+1)
   156	  runs its 3 rotated variants in one forward (yaw_rotation.py:563). `--canonicalize` + fa is refused (eval_FLAC.py:544-546).
   157	- Runner support: the runner passes any row argv verbatim, so it needs **no change**. What blocks B-F is make_cells
   158	  (vanilla flags + vanilla suffix) and the collector's vanilla expectations (finding 4). Minimal change = arm-aware
   159	  protocol in both (a constant `{BF: fa_invariant, angles, "batched", 64}`; no new manifest field needed), new blocks,
   160	  the `exp35_` name prefix, BF in `make_pairs` / `_index` / `tier2` / `tier3` / rendering, per-campaign pin. All of it is
   161	  "the cell list + the collector change"; the runner, eval_FLAC.py and src/ stay untouched.
   162	- **Tier 2 for B-F.** CANON's invariance is canonicalization (identical canonical input) and its control measures the
   163	  float residue of `canon(rot_d(md))` vs `canon(md)`. B-F's invariance is the C4 frame average: exact in exact
   164	  arithmetic for d ∈ {128, 256, 384} only, structurally absent at 45° (d = 64) and for ~99 % of random offsets
   165	  (exp_10: B-F 45° probe T60 +1.45–1.57 vs sd 0.017–0.054). The faithful analog of the composition control is the same
   166	  stagewise fixed-noise probe with A = fa(md), B = fa(rot_d(md)) on the B-F checkpoint, used as a control ONLY at
   167	  d128/d256/d384 (at d64/random the probe would measure the structural effect, not a numerical floor). That needs a
   168	  `--cond-method fa_invariant` switch in `depth_canon_cond_probe.py` (+ a BF `PROBE_CONTRACT`) — new code, ≈ 2–5 min GPU.
   169	  Options for Yixun: (A, recommended) B-F probe, C4-only control; B-F 45°/R pairs tested against the pooled-C4 floor
   170	  (deviation: the registered 45°→d64 / random→random mapping is meaningless for FA); (B, no new code) the registered
   171	  CANON control as-is → B-F's C4 pairs must be bit-exact → expected FAIL caused by the reference; (C, no new code,
   172	  descriptive) B-F's own full-split C4 pairs as the empirical floor for its 45°/R pairs. Under every option B-F's
   173	  45°/R pairs fail Tier 2 by construction; T-dup is expected to be exact (eval forward passes are expected deterministic;
   174	  exp_25's CANON T-dup K8 was bit-exact across GPU 0 → GPU 1). Tier 1 is undefined for B-F (no canonical image).
