worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_35_orbitrir_yaw_evidence_claude/orbitrir_yaw_evidence_worklog.md:5:- **Research (read-only Opus 5.5 subagent, ≈ 22:12–22:52 EST — corrected from the subagent's 22:15–23:30 stamp, whose end had not been reached; `orbitrir_yaw_evidence_research_notes.md`, file:line evidence)** — the minimal scope as written does not hold: (1) every rotated exp_10 A6 / a6c4 JSON is gone (only the per-seed CSVs remain; the paper repo's provenance file says so), and exp_10 cells carry no stream sidecar / dumps / receipt, so `depth_canon_collect.py`'s estimators (input_hash-paired) cannot use them — B-F θ=0 must be re-run at the new pin (10 cells; Yixun's 2 measurement cells are the first 2), and one-pin Δ_C4 / 45° need B-F C4+45 cells (8); (2) the cell generator and the collector hard-code vanilla and one pin → a per-arm protocol (B-F: fa_invariant, angles 0/90/180/270, cap 64) and an exp_35 collect mode reading exp_25's committed results; (3) CANON's composition control (p99 exactly 0 at quarter turns) is not a valid Tier 2 reference for a frame-averaged model → the composition probe re-run on B-F with fa conditioning, used at the C4 offsets (a small probe change); (4) **the attention backend changed after exp_25**: `flash-attn 2.7.4.post1` was installed into `flac` on Nov 1 23:14 (for exp_30); exp_25 and exp_22's P1 (Aug 19 – Oct 30 era) ran WITHOUT it, exp_07 / exp_10 WITH it → the CODE eval path is unchanged since `d6ca307a`, the numerics are not; (5) the runner aborts if HEAD moves → run from a worktree.
