Two important distinctions are emerging. First, the B-F flags are correct and the runner itself is protocol-agnostic; the required edits are in manifest generation, artifact verification, pairing, and reporting. Second, B-F Tier 2 should not reuse CANON’s zero-valued quarter-turn control: it needs a B-F/FA numerical control for C4 only, while 45° and random yaw should be reported as outside the C4 invariance claim (with dump distances), not folded into a misleading all-angle Tier 2 PASS/FAIL.
