619:- **Ambiguities resolved (each a reading, disclosed)** — (a) "Include the pinned anchor digest/query digest in evidence": published G0's whole anchor block and key-set result AND made it a G3 / G3D clause (no or unpinned anchor → FAIL / incomplete), since a published field that nothing judges would not stop a wrong anchor. (b) "serialize the complete replay-partition record": `chunk["replay_partition"]` became the record dict (contract change; its `partition` is the old list); each chunk now also carries its per-key facts and the executed partition its raw counts, because the per-key aggregate alone cannot show a key present on one side in a single chunk. (c) "recomputes every PASS clause … FROM THE SERIALIZED JSON ONLY": the verifier also checks cross-field equalities that hold by construction in the driver (comparison inputs vs the binding, declared == the binding's `fa_partition`, every summary vs its parts), so it is at least as strict as the gate on real evidence; unit-test reports finalized at fixture numbers are not real evidence and do not re-verify. (d) "G1, G2, G0 and GV if the serialized fields already allow it cheaply — say which": G1, G2, GV yes as they stood; G0 no — it needed its frozen digests per query and the published binding (two additive fields) — added rather than leave G0 out. (e) "the run summary's ledger block … equal to the ledger": exactly equal at a merge; at a reopen the summary may be absent or describe exactly a PREFIX of the segments — the only legitimate stale state (an invocation finished, a later one crashed after adding a segment); exact equality at reopen would make that crash unrecoverable. (f) "every count a non-negative integer": literal (zero admitted, bools refused), plus the canonical-serialization round trip. (g) NIT 5 "document … or stage/quarantine rows": the brief's explicit marker, not staging (staging would change the row-publication path of a 3-day pass); the marker is also written when the BEFORE-ROW check fails (a disclosed superset: same predicate family, same incomplete rows). (h) A6 (iv) "refused by merge and report": the report's refusal needed one line in `meshgrid_report.py` (no engine function reads a run directory for the report); `meshgrid_crossarm` admission inherits it. (i) HIGH 3's "`fa_partition_census` (merge and report)": read as the merge and its receipt (`merge_report.json`); the per-arm report never read the fa ledger and still does not. (j) NIT 6's `exit 1`: right for a launch script under `set -euo pipefail`; in an interactive shell it would close the terminal, so the list says to wrap the checks in `( … )` there. (k) "a provenance clause flipped": tested as a flipped provenance FACT (`tracked_clean: false`) and as a flipped `verdict_clauses.provenance` flag.
