   728	  - **A6 (iv) — a non-admissible shard** — a shard whose executed-partition check fails (the final exact check, or the check before a row) writes `partition_check_failed.json`; its rows are INCOMPLETE ARTIFACTS: `--merge-shards`, the per-arm report and the crossarm refuse it by name ("NON-ADMISSIBLE"), and so does every reopen (`--resume`, or a relaunch into the same out-dir). Fix the cause, then RESTART the shard in a fresh out-dir with fresh launch records — never resume it. A shard killed WHILE an executed-partition check ran still carries `partition_check_pending.json` (rB-F3; Codex rB-F2 NIT 5) and is non-admissible in the same way: refused by name by the merge, the per-arm report, the crossarm and every reopen; restart it. Before each merge, name both first: `for d in outputs_loc/exp22/r2_<ARM>_${TAG}_cafe outputs_loc/exp22/r2_<ARM>_${TAG}_rest15; do for f in partition_check_failed.json partition_check_pending.json; do test ! -e "$d/$f" || { echo "STOP: $d carries $f -- NON-ADMISSIBLE (A6 iv): restart it in a fresh out-dir"; exit 1; }; done; done`.
   729	  - **Ledger integrity (rB-F2 cycle 5)** — a BF shard's `fa_partition_ledger.json` is read through ONE validating reader at every reopen (the driver refuses in preflight — before the engine is built or anything is written — with `REFUSED: out-dir …: … does not verify: …`) and at the merge (nothing written). Such a refusal means the shard's executed-partition evidence no longer verifies: restart the shard; never edit a ledger or a run summary. (rB-F3) The reader also refuses: a missing ledger in an out-dir that is not FRESH (anything but the emitted launch records in it — the ledger is opened and written FIRST, before the binding, by the driver itself); a row whose ledger stamp (`fa_ledger_stamps/<room>/q<position>.json`, written just before the row) does not bind its segment's state; and, for the MERGED directory, a ledger or a `merge_report.json` receipt that do not join — the BF per-arm report re-reads the merged ledger exactly. Never edit a ledger, a stamp, a run summary or a merge report.
