worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_35_orbitrir_yaw_evidence_claude/orbitrir_yaw_evidence_yixun_query.md:7:Yixun (2026-11-04 ~14:15), NEW EXPERIMENT, approved: give the frame-averaged B-F model (OrbitRIR in the paper; exp07_BF @40k checkpoint, the one behind the `fa scratch B-F @40k` table rows and the exp_10 A6 rotation campaign) the same yaw-invariance evidence CANON has in exp_25, so CANON vs OrbitRIR can be stated on both axes. Keep it MINIMAL, no more training, one checkpoint. Plan first (short plan, Codex plan review per CLAUDE.md), implementation in Opus 5.5 max subagents, then run. (1) What already exists and must be reused, not re-run: exp_10 A6 cells for B-F and vanilla P1 at 0/45/90 (5 eval seeds, K=1 and K=8) and the a6c4 180/270 cells (analysis/yaw_robustness/generated/*.csv, outputs_FLAC/exp07_BF/...); exp_25's CANON, P1-pin and YAW-pin Tier 1-3 results at pin d6ca307a. Record in the worklog whether the exp_10 cells (legacy per-angle loop, its own pin) are admissible next to the exp_25 pin: the two agree on vanilla FLAC at theta=0 to three decimals, say so explicitly, and if the exp_25 evaluator would score B-F at theta=0 differently, measure that first (2 cells) before deciding. (2) What is missing for B-F: the exp_25 random-yaw R cells (eval seeds 42-46, K=1 and K=8, 10 cells) and a T-dup determinism cell; and Tier 2 (scored waveform dumps vs the composition control) only if it can be had cheaply at the exp_25 pin, otherwise report Tier 3 only and say so. Compute Delta_C4, the 45-deg probe, Delta_R and sd(m_Z) item-weighted exactly as depth_canon_collect.py does, and apply the registered Tier 3 rule, so B-F gets a row next to CANON, P1-pin and YAW-pin in the same spread table. Evaluator: the exp_25 pin d6ca307a (or the current localization-exp HEAD if you show the eval path is unchanged since the pin), fa_invariant cond-method for B-F, num_samples 6337, recipe unchanged. (3) Cards: run the cells as a co-tenant on GPU 1 after today's exp_30 seed-44 tables finish (~16:30), ahead of the exp_22 GPU tests and gates; check memory headroom first and do not slow my exp_30 seed-43 training more than the s44 tables did. Give me an ETA. (4) Deliverable: a results file with (a) ONE table (not two) of Vanilla FLAC, CANON and OrbitRIR B-F with the six metrics (T60, C50, EDT, R@1, R@5, R@10) at K=1 and K=8 on unseen AR at theta=0; (b) the same six metrics at 45 deg and under random yaw for the three models; (c) the Tier 3 spread table with B-F added. New experiment number, worklog entry, commit on localization-exp. Report in this pane when the plan is ready and again when the cells are done.
